course: dictionary
lesson: 4345
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Guidance» is one of these words. «The teacher gave me guidance on how to write my story.» Here guidance means help and advice about what to do.
explain: «The guidance puts getting back to school and learning before getting back to sport.» This guidance is not personal advice from one person. It is official instructions from a group. Ask yourself who is giving it and what it is for. The clues are the words around it: school, learning and sport.
explain: Guidance can also be a technical word for the system that steers a rocket or vehicle. Only the context can tell you which meaning is right. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: Guidance means help and advice about what to do or how to behave.
fact: Guidance can also mean official instructions or rules from an official group.
fact: In technical use, guidance is the system that steers a rocket, missile or vehicle.
fact: Guidance is uncountable, so you say «some guidance», not «a guidance» or «guidances».
fact: Useful phrases include «under the guidance of», «guidance counsellor» and «parental guidance».
exercise: «The teacher gave me guidance on how to write my story.» What does guidance mean here? | *Help and advice about what to do | A system that steers a rocket | A rule about how many goals to score
exercise: «UK guidance says children should be active for at least 60 minutes a day.» What kind of guidance is this? | *Official instructions from an official group | Personal advice from a friend | A steering system for a vehicle
exercise: Which sentence uses guidance correctly? | She gave me three guidances. | She gave me a guidance. | *She gave me some guidance.
test: «The rocket's guidance system kept it on course.» Which meaning of guidance fits here? | *The system that steers a rocket | Help and advice from a teacher | Kind words from a friend | Official rules about sport
test: What is a guidance counsellor? | A teacher who coaches football | *Someone at school who helps pupils | A rocket engineer | A film rating for young audiences
exam: «If in doubt, sit them out» is UK guidance for sport. Which meaning of guidance does this show? | Help about homework | *Official instructions from an official group | A word meaning a short walk | Steering a car
